Validation and visualisation rules (backend/vendor/)
====================================================

KoSIT validator configuration for XRechnung
  What:     UBL 2.1 and UN/CEFACT CII D16B XML schemas, the compiled
            EN 16931 (CEN) and XRechnung Schematron rules as XSLT, and
            scenarios.xml
  Where:    backend/vendor/xrechnung-config/
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0 (backend/vendor/xrechnung-config/LICENSE).
            The folder's own NOTICE file is retained unchanged; it reads
            "KoSIT XML-Validator Configuration for XRechnung, Copyright 2020
            Koordinierungsstelle für IT-Standards" and credits the
            Coordination Office for IT-Standards (http://www.xoev.de/).
            The LICENSE file also carries a German note that EN 16931 is
            copyright of CEN, that XRechnung implements its semantic data
            model and two mandatory syntaxes, and that reproduction is
            permitted by CEN and DIN as copyright holders.
  Source:   https://github.com/itplr-kosit/validator-configuration-xrechnung
  Version:  release tag v2026-01-31, asset
            xrechnung-3.0.2-validator-configuration-2026-01-31.zip
            (XRechnung 3.0.2)
  Bundled third-party parts, as listed in the folder's README.md (the
  README states no separate licence for them, so each is used as
  distributed in the KoSIT release):
    - XML Schema of UBL Invoice and CreditNote 2.1 (OASIS,
      http://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/os-UBL-2.1/), in resources/ubl/2.1/xsd/
    - XML Schema of UN/CEFACT uncoupled version 16B (UN/CEFACT,
      http://www.unece.org/cefact/xml_schemas/index.html),
      in resources/cii/16b/xsd/
    - Schematron of EN16931:2017
      (https://github.com/ConnectingEurope/eInvoicing-EN16931),
      in resources/ubl/2.1/xsl/ and resources/cii/16b/xsl/
    - Schematron of CIUS XRechnung, Extension XRechnung and CIUS XRechnung
      CVD (KoSIT, https://projekte.kosit.org/xrechnung/xrechnung-schematron/),
      in resources/xrechnung/3.0.2/xsl/

