Downloaded at run time, not in the repository
=============================================

These artefacts are used by Eingang's tools but are neither committed nor
bundled into any build. They are listed so a reader knows where they come
from and under which terms they are used.

ZUGFeRD corpus (full corpus)
  What:     Sample e-invoices used by parsing tests and the evaluation
  Where:    Downloaded by `uv run poe fetch-corpus`
            (backend/tools/fetch_corpus.py) into data/corpus/, which is
            git-ignored. Only file names, SHA-256 hashes and metadata of
            the selected documents are committed, in
            evals/data/manifest.json.
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0
  Source:   https://github.com/ZUGFeRD/corpus
  Version:  commit d891458e9822e34271a5438497bf924e89955979

KoSIT validator
  What:     The official Java validator, used only by the validation
            parity evaluation (evals/parity.py), together with the full
            XRechnung validator configuration release zip
  Where:    Downloaded by `uv run poe eval-parity` into data/kosit/, which
            is git-ignored, and checked against pinned SHA-256 hashes. It
            runs in the eclipse-temurin:21-jre Docker image.
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0
  Source:   https://github.com/itplr-kosit/validator
  Version:  v1.6.0 (validator-1.6.0.zip); configuration release v2026-01-31

Swagger UI
  What:     The API documentation page at /docs
  Where:    Loaded by the visitor's browser from
            https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/swagger-ui-dist@5.33.1; not
            served or bundled by Eingang
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0
  Source:   https://github.com/swagger-api/swagger-ui
  Version:  5.33.1

Docker base images and Python packages
  The images named in compose.yaml and the Dockerfiles (postgres,
  temporalio/temporal, python, ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv, node,
  eclipse-temurin) are pulled from their registries when an image is
  built or a container starts; this repository does not redistribute
  them. Python packages are installed from PyPI at the versions in
  backend/uv.lock and are not vendored.
